  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ashoka | Dashmake Emergency Response Mobile App Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Health/Techo. Beneficiaries: 12229 (including 4328 women). Description: SOS System is a multi-service platform for optimizing the efficiency of first responders&apos; interventions at the scene of a disaster. Thanks to the SOS Mobile application, a witness or a victim of a disaster could, at the touch of a button, declare the disaster and send information about it. A discussion (video or audio) is triggered between the rescuer (at the switchboard) and the witness in order to give first aid advice to the victim. SOS Bracelet, the digital health record, allows emergency doctors to access the victim&apos;s health history in order to improve emergency care.</narrative>
  </description>
